:question
$()We have 3 differentiable functions 
!insmath f
$(), 
!insmath g
$()	and 
!insmath h
$(),	with values and derivatives shown in the following table.	 <table class="wimscenter wimsborder">	<tr><th>x</th><th>-3</th><th>-2</th><th>-1</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath f(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val7</td><td>$val8</td><td>$val9</td><td>$val10</td><td>$val11</td><td>$val12</td><td>$val13</td></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath f '(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val14</td><td>$val15</td><td>$val16</td><td>$val17</td><td>$val18</td><td>$val19</td><td>$val20</td></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath g(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val21</td><td>$val22</td><td>$val23</td><td>$val24</td><td>$val25</td><td>$val26</td><td>$val27</td></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath g'(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val28</td><td>$val29</td><td>$val30</td><td>$val31</td><td>$val32</td><td>$val33</td><td>$val34</td></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath h(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val35</td><td>$val36</td><td>$val37</td><td>$val38</td><td>$val39</td><td>$val40</td><td>$val41</td></tr>	<tr><th>
!insmath h'(x)
$()</th>	<td>$val42</td><td>$val43</td><td>$val44</td><td>$val45</td><td>$val46</td><td>$val47</td><td>$val48</td></tr>	</table>	Let 
!insmath s
$() the function defined by 
!insmath s(x) = f(g(h(x)))
$(). Compute the derivative	
!insmath s'($val49)
$().	
$()
